# ⚠ RETIRED — secrets now come from Bitwarden Secrets Manager at run time and
# there is no vault.yml (docs/decisions/0027-control-node-secrets-bws-runtime.md). These patterns
# stay as a backstop so a leftover file from before the migration, or one
# created out of habit, can never be committed.
# Glob the suffix too: a rename-aside during the migration (vault.yml.bkp,
# .bak, .old) is exactly the "leftover file" case, and the un-suffixed patterns
# missed it — leaving an encrypted blob of every credential untracked in the
# tree, one `git add -A` from being committed permanently.
inventory/group_vars/all/vault.yml*
inventory/group_vars/**/vault.yml*
.vault-pass

# One-shot vault->BWS migration output (playbooks/port-vault-to-secrets.yml).
# One plaintext file per secret, 0600 in a 0700 dir. Delete once ported.
.bws-port/

# Transpiled artifacts / build scratch
*.ign

# Fetched cluster kubeconfig (playbooks/bootstrap-cluster.yml writes it here with
# the server URL rewritten to the DMZ IP). Holds cluster-admin client certs —
# NEVER commit. Regenerated on demand from the running node's /etc/rancher/k3s.
.kube/

# Rendered pfSense/FRR config (playbooks/render-frr-config.yml). frr.conf
# embeds the FRR master password (from BWS), so it's a credential-bearing
# artifact — NEVER commit. Regenerate on demand from inventory/nodes.yml + BWS; the
# committed inputs are the template and the node map, not this output.
.frr/

# Rendered Proxmox-Ceph setup scripts (playbooks/render-ceph-setup.yml). They
# embed ceph_fs_name (a vaulted storage name), and ceph-k8s-keys.sh PRINTS the
# two cephx keys when run — so this is a credential-adjacent artifact. NEVER
# commit. Regenerate on demand; the committed inputs are the templates and
# group_vars, not this output. Procedure: docs/proxmox-ceph-k8s-setup.md
.ceph/

# In-repo Ansible collections path (collections_path in ansible.cfg). Restored
# from requirements.yml via `uv run ansible-galaxy collection install`, like the
# uv venv is from uv.lock — the pinned input is requirements.yml, not this tree.
.ansible/
